From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:54:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: describe the video encoder and its
 DARTs

Add the AVE2 video encoder and its two DART instances from the J604
runtime ADT (/arm-io/ave, /arm-io/dart-ave):

  ave       0x421100000 +0x45c000  codec
            0x421800000 +0x800000  coprocessor
            0x421050000 +0x4000    mailbox
            0x380708000 +0x4000    PMGR page of the VENC power states
            0x420000000 +0x1000000 (role unknown)
            irqs 970, 964, 963, 966, 965
            pre-loaded __TEXT 0x148000 / __DATA 0x12c000
            power gates VENC-SYS-V, VENC-AVE-VNOM/VMAX, VENC-MEM-FAST,
            VENC_PIPE4, VENC_PIPE5, VENC-ME0-V, VENC-ME1-V, VENC-DMA-V
  dart-ave  0x421080000 +0xc000, 0x4210a0000 +0xc000 (two instances),
            irq 967, stream 0 (mapper-ave), vm-base 0x10000000000,
            vm-size 0x30000000000, no power gate

This is the T6041 encoder's shape (codec, mailbox and coprocessor at the
same offsets from the block, the same codec size and interrupt order),
so the node follows the T6041 one: reg-names codec, mailbox, coproc,
then pmgr and the unknown window, and the five power states dma, pipe4,
pipe5, me0 and me1 (ps_venc_dma's parent is ps_venc_sys). The DARTs have
no ADT power gate; they are placed in ps_venc_dma, which keeps VENC_SYS
on as its parent, rather than in ps_venc_sys alone, so a DART is never
touched with the DMA block off.

All three nodes are "disabled", and the VENC power states stay disabled
in t8132-j604-pmgr.dtsi, so nothing probes and no power state changes.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5

[j604-int: 1.610 int after j604/k609-scaler: t8132.dtsi, both insert their nodes after jpeg1_dart, before the SEP
 DART comment. Kept both: the scaler block first, then this AVE block (53 lines, unchanged). No other hunk touched.]

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 53 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 53 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index d685fae157..7fecf0f809 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -833,6 +833,59 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Video encoder (AVE2): J604 runtime ADT ave and dart-ave. The ADT
+		 * reg order is codec, coproc, mailbox, PMGR VENC page, then a 16 MiB
+		 * window of unknown role; named here as the driver and the T6041
+		 * node expect. dart-ave has two instances sharing irq 967, stream
+		 * 0 (mapper-ave), vm-base 0x10000000000, vm-size 0x30000000000 and
+		 * no power gate of its own: it is put in the VENC DMA domain (a
+		 * child of VENC_SYS) so both are on whenever a DART is touched.
+		 */
+		ave: video-codec@421100000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-ave", "apple,ave";
+			reg = <0x4 0x21100000 0x0 0x45c000>,
+			      <0x4 0x21050000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x4 0x21800000 0x0 0x800000>,
+			      <0x3 0x80708000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x4 0x20000000 0x0 0x1000000>;
+			reg-names = "codec", "mailbox", "coproc", "pmgr", "fabric";
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 970 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <AIC_IRQ 964 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <AIC_IRQ 963 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <AIC_IRQ 966 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <AIC_IRQ 965 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_venc_dma>, <&ps_venc_pipe4>,
+					<&ps_venc_pipe5>, <&ps_venc_me0>,
+					<&ps_venc_me1>;
+			power-domain-names = "dma", "pipe4", "pipe5", "me0", "me1";
+			iommus = <&ave_dart0 0>, <&ave_dart1 0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		ave_dart0: iommu@421080000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
+			reg = <0x4 0x21080000 0x0 0xc000>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 967 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+			apple,dma-range = <0x100 0x0 0x300 0x0>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_venc_dma>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		ave_dart1: iommu@4210a0000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
+			reg = <0x4 0x210a0000 0x0 0xc000>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 967 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+			apple,dma-range = <0x100 0x0 0x300 0x0>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_venc_dma>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		/*
 		 * The SEP DART's input aperture is the BIT(40) alias the DART
 		 * translates (ADT vm-base-0 0x10000004000).
